===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*swerdą||literally ‘cutting, festering thing’}}, of uncertain origin, possibly from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*seh₂w-||sharp}}.
Cognate with {{cog|ofs|swerd}} (West Frisian {{m|fy|swurd}}), Old Saxon {{m|osx|swerd}} (Low German {{m|nds|Sweerd}}), Old Dutch {{m|odt|swert}} (Dutch ''[[zwaard]])'', Old High German {{m|goh|swert}} (German ''[[Schwert]]''), Old Norse {{m|non|sverð}} (Danish ''[[sværd]]'', Norwegian ''[[sverd]]'', Swedish ''[[svärd]])''

